# Defence in depth for the shadowing hazard documented in jwt.py.
#
# `Dockerfile` does `COPY . .` into `WORKDIR /app`, which precedes site-packages
# on sys.path. Any top-level module here that shares a name with an installed
# package silently outranks it. `jwt.py` did exactly that and disabled
# authentication in the image.
#
# jwt.py is now inert by default, so this is belt-and-braces rather than the
# fix — but the file has no reason to be in a production image at all.
jwt.py

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
